# Unity .gitignore Template
# Source: https://github.com/github/gitignore/blob/main/Unity.gitignore
# Last synced: 2025-12-18
# License: CC0-1.0
#
# This template is maintained from the github/gitignore repository
# and distributed under Creative Commons Zero v1.0 Universal license.

# This .gitignore file should be placed at the root of your Unity project directory
#
# Get latest from https://github.com/github/gitignore/blob/main/Unity.gitignore
#
.utmp/
/[Ll]ibrary/
/[Tt]emp/
/[Oo]bj/
/[Bb]uild/
/[Bb]uilds/
/[Ll]ogs/
/[Uu]ser[Ss]ettings/
*.log

# By default unity supports Blender asset imports, *.blend1 blender files do not need to be committed to version control.
*.blend1
*.blend1.meta

# MemoryCaptures can get excessive in size.
# They also could contain extremely sensitive data
/[Mm]emoryCaptures/

# Recordings can get excessive in size
/[Rr]ecordings/

# Uncomment this line if you wish to ignore the asset store tools plugin
# /[Aa]ssets/AssetStoreTools*

# Autogenerated Jetbrains Rider plugin
/[Aa]ssets/Plugins/Editor/JetBrains*
# Jetbrains Rider personal-layer settings
*.DotSettings.user

# Visual Studio cache directory
.vs/

# Gradle cache directory
.gradle/

# Autogenerated VS/MD/Consulo solution and project files
ExportedObj/
.consulo/
*.csproj
*.unityproj
*.sln
*.suo
*.tmp
*.user
*.userprefs
*.pidb
*.booproj
*.svd
*.pdb
*.mdb
*.opendb
*.VC.db

# Unity3D generated meta files
*.pidb.meta
*.pdb.meta
*.mdb.meta

# Unity3D generated file on crash reports
sysinfo.txt

# Mono auto generated files
mono_crash.*

# Builds
*.apk
*.aab
*.unitypackage
*.unitypackage.meta
*.app

# Crashlytics generated file
crashlytics-build.properties

# TestRunner generated files
InitTestScene*.unity*

# Addressables default ignores, before user customizations
/ServerData
/[Aa]ssets/StreamingAssets/aa*
/[Aa]ssets/AddressableAssetsData/link.xml*
/[Aa]ssets/Addressables_Temp*
# By default, Addressables content builds will generate addressables_content_state.bin
# files in platform-specific subfolders, for example:
# /Assets/AddressableAssetsData/OSX/addressables_content_state.bin
/[Aa]ssets/AddressableAssetsData/*/*.bin*

# Visual Scripting auto-generated files
/[Aa]ssets/Unity.VisualScripting.Generated/VisualScripting.Flow/UnitOptions.db
/[Aa]ssets/Unity.VisualScripting.Generated/VisualScripting.Flow/UnitOptions.db.meta
/[Aa]ssets/Unity.VisualScripting.Generated/VisualScripting.Core/Property Providers
/[Aa]ssets/Unity.VisualScripting.Generated/VisualScripting.Core/Property Providers.meta

# Auto-generated scenes by play mode tests
/[Aa]ssets/[Ii]nit[Tt]est[Ss]cene*.unity*

# Test-run output from headless Unity runs (agents and CI write results XML + logs here).
# NOT part of the project: ignoring it keeps `git status` readable and, more importantly, stops
# these ever being swept into a commit by an over-broad `git add`.
/artifacts/

# Stray hooks folder created when a `git lfs install` gets redirected to a literal `dev/null`
# path on Windows (Git Bash makes it a real directory). Harmless duplicate of .git/hooks.
/dev/

# The CLIFF FACE KIT's baked pixels (Assets/_Project/Art/Terrain/Cliffs/) are COMMITTED, under LFS
# (*.png), since terrain-fidelity P1 (11-07). They were ignored here until then, and that broke
# every clone: the walls name their faces by .meta GUID, a bake from nothing minted fresh GUIDs,
# so a clone, CI and a build drew the St Peters and Nine Mile Creek cliffs with no face. CliffBaker
# now writes each GUID from the file's place in the kit (CliffFaceGuidTests holds it), and a
# re-bake after a rig edit is a PR that re-commits what it wrote (~9.6 MB for all three rocks).

# The NMC ROAD FLOOR's baked chunks (`node tools/nmc-roads/bake-chunks.cjs` over the committed
# network file). DELIBERATELY NOT COMMITTED, as the cliff face kit was until 11-07: 3,744 PNGs (1,248 each
# of normal, light and detail) = 160 MB, every byte regenerable by the builder and stale the moment
# the network or the kit moves. The manifest RoadFloor.json and the folder metas ARE committed;
# RoadFloorManifestTests reads the manifest and ignores when it is absent; RoadFloorStreamer reads
# the PNGs at runtime. NineMileCreekSceneRoutesTests' four floor cases ignore when the PNGs are absent.
# A fresh clone renders the road floor untextured until the bake is run once.
/[Aa]ssets/StreamingAssets/RoadFloor/NineMileCreek/*.png
/[Aa]ssets/StreamingAssets/RoadFloor/NineMileCreek/*.png.meta

# ADR 0047: terrain arrays are recipe import artifacts in Library.
/[Aa]ssets/_Project/Art/Terrain/Derived/
/[Aa]ssets/_Project/Art/Terrain/Derived.meta

# Python bytecode from the standalone tools under tools/ (they run outside Unity, so nothing
# else in the repo would otherwise mention Python).
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]

# The audio lane's working area: downloaded sources, the build scripts, and the
# intermediate renders. The COMMITTED audio is the small set under
# Assets/_Project/Audio/ with a row each in that folder's LICENSES.md; the raw
# downloads behind them are hundreds of MB and regenerable from the URLs in that
# ledger, so they stay out of a public repository.
/_inbox/

# The PRIVATE SOUND PACK's copies (Hidden Harbours ▸ Audio ▸ Install Private Sound Pack).
#
# ⭐ DELIBERATELY NOT COMMITTED. These sounds are licensed to the owner alone, so they may never reach
# this public repository. AudioClipSets lays Private/Resources/AudioClipSetPrivate over the public
# clip set at boot; without this folder the public set plays exactly as it is and the music bus is
# silent. AudioClipSetsTests guards both lines below (docs/audio/private-sound-pack.md).
/[Aa]ssets/_Project/Audio/Private/
/[Aa]ssets/_Project/Audio/Private.meta
